From: rudi193-cmd <rudi193-cmd@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 17:01:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gh-NNNNN: Skip VSOCK stream test when the transport reports
 ENODEV

On a VSOCK guest whose transport cannot reach its own CID, connect()
fails with ENODEV and the server side of ThreadedVSOCKSocketStreamTest
waits in accept() until LOOPBACK_TIMEOUT, so the test errors instead
of skipping. Probe a connection to the local CID in setUp() and skip
on ENODEV.

Every added line is taken verbatim from CPython as of dcb1caef5bd8
(2021-06-28).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RZg885hiYVZjnaq6h1v2x6
---
 Lib/test/test_socket.py | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Lib/test/test_socket.py b/Lib/test/test_socket.py
index cd07e94..e316b2c 100644
--- a/Lib/test/test_socket.py
+++ b/Lib/test/test_socket.py
@@ -569,6 +569,14 @@ def __init__(self, methodName='runTest'):
         ThreadableTest.__init__(self)
 
     def setUp(self):
+        self.cli = socket.socket(socket.AF_VSOCK, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
+        self.addCleanup(self.cli.close)
+        cid = get_cid()
+        try:
+            self.cli.connect((cid, VSOCKPORT))
+        except OSError as e:
+            if e.errno == errno.ENODEV:
+                self.skipTest(str(e))
         self.serv = socket.socket(socket.AF_VSOCK, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
         self.addCleanup(self.serv.close)
         self.serv.bind((socket.VMADDR_CID_ANY, VSOCKPORT))
